    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0323" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg249"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 23, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 16th
                    ultimo, No. 32, which is ac companied by a copy of your note of the 3d of the
                    same month to M. Miguet, the perpetual secretary of the Academy of Moral and
                    Political Sciences, and a translation of his reply of the 11th in relation to
                    the death of the Hon. Edward Everett. Your thoughtfulness in making the
                    communication, and the manner in which it was done, are highly appreciated, as
                    are the sensibility and respect evinced by the academy upon learning that death
                    had stricken from its rolls our distinguished countryman.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
